<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Magic of Etheria (old)</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;*This work is in the process of being rewritten*&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lance and George supplied the stack of blank books as promised, fulfilling their end of the favour - for now. They stand, tall and patient, piled high at one end of the desk. Adora adjusts her dress to a more comfortable position before wiggling in her chair. She supposes she's going to be here for a while. After all, there's a lot to think about...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Where to begin? She ponders. At the beginning, she decides.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;And after that? An adventure beyond anything she could have imagined. From the long-lost depths to the magical skies of Etheria. With the Horde truly gone, the rebuilding is all but complete. But that wasn't the case back then. Adora smiles at the thought of Catra; she was there that morning, quite unexpectedly. That was before they knew about her magic, before she learnt to control it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora takes a final deep breath, thinking about everything they've been through since the Heart. It's all important, the good days, the bad days; she'll write about them all. With that thought in mind, she reaches for the first of the blank books and, after opening it to the first page, puts pen to paper...&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>IorekoftheHorde</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
